## Heartbeat-Driven State Reconciliation Engine

To avoid split-brain execution and prevent stuck tool invocation leases when an active worker thread freezes, crashes, or suffers from high GC/kernel pause events, ATEP mandates a periodic bidirectional heartbeat state machine. Workers lease intents for a fixed duration ($T_{\text{lease}}$). If a worker fails to renew its epoch heartbeat prior to lease decay, the control plane forcefully transitions the tool execution state from `EXECUTING` to `LEASE_EXPIRED`, revoking worker authority and making the intent eligible for automatic steal-and-replay.

```
       ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │                                                        │
       ▼                                                        │
[ SLOT_EMPTY ] ──(Enqueue)──► [ SLOT_READY ] ──(Dequeue)──► [ EXECUTING ]
       ▲                                                        │
       │                                            (Heartbeat Timeout)
       │                                                        │
       │                                                        ▼
[ COMMITTED ] ◄──(Reconcile Success)─── [ RECONCILING ] ◄─(Revoke Authority)
```

### Reconciliation State Machine Implementation

```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;
use std::sync::RwLock;
use std::time::{Duration, Instant};

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ExecutionState {
    Ready,
    Executing { worker_id: u64, lease_deadline: Instant },
    Reconciling,
    Committed,
    Aborted,
}

pub struct HeartbeatReconciler {
    leases: RwLock<HashMap<u64, (u64, Instant)>>, // Maps sequence_id -> (worker_id, lease_deadline)
    lease_ttl: Duration,
}

impl HeartbeatReconciler {
    pub fn new(lease_ttl: Duration) -> Self {
        Self {
            leases: RwLock::new(HashMap::new()),
            lease_ttl,
        }
    }

    /// Registers a tool intent execution lease for a given worker.
    pub fn register_lease(&self, sequence_id: u64, worker_id: u64) {
        let mut guard = self.leases.write().unwrap();
        let deadline = Instant::now() + self.lease_ttl;
        guard.insert(sequence_id, (worker_id, deadline));
    }

    /// Extends an active lease if the worker matches and lease has not lapsed.
    pub fn process_heartbeat(&self, sequence_id: u64, worker_id: u64) -> bool {
        let mut guard = self.leases.write().unwrap();
        if let Some((active_worker, deadline)) = guard.get_mut(&sequence_id) {
            if *active_worker == worker_id && Instant::now() < *deadline {
                *deadline = Instant::now() + self.lease_ttl;
                return true;
            }
        }
        false
    }

    /// Scans active leases and revokes expired work items for state recovery.
    pub fn sweep_expired_leases(&self) -> Vec<u64> {
        let mut guard = self.leases.write().unwrap();
        let now = Instant::now();
        let mut expired = Vec::new();

        guard.retain(|seq_id, (_, deadline)| {
            if now >= *deadline {
                expired.push(*seq_id);
                false // Evict from active lease map
            } else {
                true
            }
        });

        expired
    }
}
```

