## Operational Invariants & Protocol Formalization

To ensure invariant safety proofs hold under arbitrary asynchronous scheduling, packet drops, and thread disruptions, ATEP maintains three strict mathematical invariants across the runtime pipeline:

1. **At-Most-Once Execution Invariant ($I_1$)**:
   $$\forall s \in \text{SequenceIDs}, \quad \sum_{w \in \text{Workers}} \mathbb{I}(\text{State}(s, w) = \text{EXECUTING}) \le 1$$
   No intent sequence $s$ shall ever execute simultaneously on multiple worker threads regardless of lock contention.

2. **Zero-Loss Durability Invariant ($I_2$)**:
   $$\text{Frame}_{\text{Enqueued}}(s) \implies \left( s \in \text{WAL}_{\text{Committed}} \lor s \in \text{RingBuffer}_{\text{Ready}} \right)$$
   Every acknowledged frame must reside in persistent append-only storage before tail-pointer pointer publishing.

3. **Bounded Delay State Liveness Invariant ($I_3$)**:
   $$\lim_{t \to \infty} P\left( \text{State}_t(s) \in \{ \text{COMMITTED}, \text{ABORTED} \} \right) = 1$$
   Every intent is guaranteed to eventually resolve to a terminal execution state within $T_{\text{max}} = T_{\text{lease}} + T_{\text{reconcile}}$.

### Protocol State Transition Matrix

| Current State | Next State | Trigger Event | Atomic Barrier | Safety Invariant Enforced |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `SLOT_EMPTY` | `SLOT_WRITING` | Publisher CAS Claim | `Acquire` | Slot Collision Prevention |
| `SLOT_WRITING` | `SLOT_READY` | Frame Transferred & WAL Synced | `Release` | Memory Ordering Visiblity |
| `SLOT_READY` | `SLOT_READING` | Dequeue CAS Target | `Acquire` | Single-Consumer Exclusion |
| `SLOT_READING` | `EXECUTING` | Lease Issued | `AcqRel` | $I_1$ (At-Most-Once Execution) |
| `EXECUTING` | `LEASE_EXPIRED` | $t > T_{\text{lease}}$ Timeout | `SeqCst` | Stale Execution Eviction |
| `LEASE_EXPIRED`| `RECONCILING` | Controller Intervention | `SeqCst` | Reclaim Authority |
| `RECONCILING` | `SLOT_READY` | Automated Replay | `Release` | $I_2$ (Zero-Loss Durability) |
| `EXECUTING` | `COMMITTED` | Success Completion Signal | `Release` | Terminal State Finalization |

