## 4. Concurrency, Sharding & High-Availability Boundaries

To scale horizontally without lock contention, the auction engine shards state deterministically across available CPU hardware threads using core pinning (`pthread_setaffinity_np`). Memory structures follow a strict thread-per-core non-blocking model.

```
                          +-----------------------------------+
                          |   NIC Transmit/Receive Rings      |
                          +-----------------------------------+
                                    /               \\
                          eBPF RSS /                 \\ eBPF RSS
                                  /                   \\
                                 v                     v
                  +---------------------+       +---------------------+
                  | CPU Core 0 (Shard 0)|       | CPU Core 1 (Shard 1)|
                  | Lock-Free MPMC Ring |       | Lock-Free MPMC Ring |
                  | Local Price Oracle  |       | Local Price Oracle  |
                  +---------------------+       +---------------------+
                                 \\                     /
                                  \\                   /
                                   v                 v
                          +-----------------------------------+
                          | Core-Cross Sync Engine (CAS Loop) |
                          +-----------------------------------+
```

### Lock-Free Memory Engine Implementation

The central compute ring maintains high-performance execution guarantees through atomic state transition primitives written in Rust:

```rust
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, AtomicUsize, Ordering};
use std::ptr;

pub struct LockFreeAuctionRing<T, const N: usize> {
    buffer: [*mut T; N],
    head: AtomicUsize,
    tail: AtomicUsize,
    current_clearing_price: AtomicU64,
}

unsafe impl<T: Send, const N: usize> Sync for LockFreeAuctionRing<T, N> {}

impl<T, const N: usize> LockFreeAuctionRing<T, N> {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        assert!(N.is_power_of_two(), "Ring buffer capacity must be a power of two");
        Self {
            buffer: [ptr::null_mut(); N],
            head: AtomicUsize::new(0),
            tail: AtomicUsize::new(0),
            current_clearing_price: AtomicU64::new(100), // Default base price
        }
    }

    pub fn push(&self, item: *mut T, bid: u64) -> Result<(), *mut T> {
        let price = self.current_clearing_price.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        if bid < price {
            return Err(item); // Reject payload immediately if bid is lower than market price
        }

        let mut current_tail = self.tail.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        loop {
            let current_head = self.head.load(Ordering::Acquire);
            if current_tail.wrapping_add(1) - current_head > N {
                return Err(item); // Ring buffer full
            }

            match self.tail.compare_exchange_weak(
                current_tail,
                current_tail.wrapping_add(1),
                Ordering::AcqRel,
                Ordering::Relaxed,
            ) {
                Ok(_) => {
                    let index = current_tail & (N - 1);
                    unsafe {
                        let elem_ptr = self.buffer.as_ptr().add(index) as *mut *mut T;
                        ptr::write_volatile(elem_ptr, item);
                    }
                    self.recalculate_market_price(current_tail.wrapping_add(1) - current_head);
                    return Ok(());
                }
                Err(actual) => current_tail = actual,
            }
        }
    }

    #[inline]
    fn recalculate_market_price(&self, occupancy: usize) {
        let saturation_ratio = occupancy as f64 / N as f64;
        if saturation_ratio > 0.85 {
            let price_factor = 1.0 / (1.0 - saturation_ratio + 0.01);
            let new_price = (100.0 * price_factor) as u64;
            self.current_clearing_price.store(new_price, Ordering::Release);
        } else {
            self.current_clearing_price.store(100, Ordering::Release);
        }
```


