### Architectural Invariants

1. **Zero Cold-Boot Overhead**: Worker nodes maintain a memory-mapped, immutable golden snapshot of the agent execution context. Branch instantiation must complete within $\le 2.5\text{ ms}$ using copy-on-write page-table manipulation.
2. **Kernel Boundary Determinism**: MicroVM environments enforce deterministic clocking via paravirtualized hardware timers (`kvm-clock`) and strict trapping of monotonic time instructions (`RDTSC`/`RDTSCP`), eliminating wall-clock jitter across parallel runs [2].
3. **Lock-Free Trace Transit**: Host-to-guest and guest-to-evaluator telemetry streams must never execute synchronous heap allocation or OS context switches on the critical path, guaranteeing constant $O(1)$ telemetry pipeline latency.
4. **Quorum Non-Repudiation**: Evaluator judgments are cryptographically bound to the cryptographic hash of the execution trace, preventing selective metric forgery via BLS12-381 threshold signatures.

