## 5. Failure Modes & Chaos Engineering

To achieve operational resilience under high rollout churn, the fabric implements explicit containment mechanics against core runtime failure vectors:

### Failure Modes & Mitigation Matrix

| Failure Mode | Root Cause Dynamic | Detection Mechanism | Automated Mitigation / Self-Healing |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **vCPU Execution Deadlock** | Agent binary enters infinite recursive branch or un-trapped spin-wait. | Watchdog timer tracking monotonic instruction counter via guest PMU. | Hard `KVM_RUN` termination signal; context tear-down and snapshot revert within $<1\text{ ms}$. |
| **Shared Memory Saturation** | Consumer trace processor halts or hits memory pressure, stalling the ring buffer. | Atomic difference: `tail - head >= capacity`. | Instantaneous drop of non-essential perceptual tensors; preservation of state transition invariants. |
| **Evaluator Judge Collusion** | Stochastic drift or semantic poisoning in downstream LLM judges skewing metrics. | Statistical distribution divergence via Kolmogorov-Smirnov test against baseline window. | Automatic disqualification of skewed judge node; dynamic quorum re-weighting via BFT protocol. |
| **Host Dirty Page Exhaustion** | Heavy page modifications across deep rollout trees deplete 2MB HugePage reserves. | Kernel `cgroupv2` memory controller notifications and userfaultfd drop events. | Eviction of least-recently-executed (LRE) speculative rollout branches; immediate memory compaction. |

### Chaos Engineering Protocols

To continuously validate fabric stability, chaos injectors execute the following runtime disruptions:
1. **Random Memory Invalidation**: Injecting bitflips into uncommitted CoW shadow pages to verify that the validation plane fails closed with an unrecoverable hash mismatch rather than propagating corrupt metric sets.
2. **Arbitrary Syscall Hijacking**: Intercepting and corrupting guest system calls via eBPF probes to confirm that anomalous agent actions never leak beyond the isolated microVM boundary into host namespace registers.
3. **Consensus Partitioning**: Simulating network link drops between evaluator nodes to verify that speculative rollouts buffer cleanly without compromising global metric commit rates.

