### Data Plane Execution & Inline WRPKRU Fast-Path

Once the control plane establishes page-table permissions and attaches eBPF telemetry hooks, data plane execution transitions into a purely userspace-driven context switch. Traditional isolation models incur a ~1,000 to 3,000 cycle penalty via system call overhead or VM-exit (`VMRUN`/`VMRESUME`). By utilizing Memory Protection Keys (`pkeys`), the supervisor context mutates thread-local memory access rights in **< 10 cycles** via the `WRPKRU` unprivileged CPU instruction.

The hardware register `PKRU` (Protection Key Rights Register for Userspace) is a 32-bit CPU register. Each key ($PK_0 \dots PK_{15}$) is allocated a 2-bit field within `PKRU`:
* **Bit $2i$ (AD):** Access Disable (blocks both read and write access).
* **Bit $2i+1$ (WD):** Write Disable (blocks write access, allows read access).

```
 31                                                                0
+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+
|AD|WD|AD|WD| ... |AD|WD|AD|WD|AD|WD|AD|WD|AD|WD|AD|WD|AD|WD|AD|WD|
| PK15| PK14| ... |  PK5|  PK4|  PK3|  PK2|  PK1|  PK0 (Supervisor)|
+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+
```

To enter an untrusted sandbox executing within $PK_1$, the supervisor updates `PKRU` to disable access to all host memory domains ($PK_0, PK_2 \dots PK_{15}$) while enabling full read/write permissions for $PK_1$.

```c
// High-Frequency Context Switch Mechanics (Userspace Fast-Path)
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <signal.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

#define CACHE_LINE_SIZE 64
#define RING_CAPACITY 1024

// Force PKRU direct write via inline assembly (Zero Kernel Trap)
static inline void __wrpkru(uint32_t pkru_val) {
    uint32_t eax = pkru_val;
    uint32_t ecx = 0; // ECX must be zero for WRPKRU execution
    uint32_t edx = 0; // EDX holds the upper 32 bits (reserved, set to 0)

    __asm__ __volatile__(
        "wrpkru"
        : 
        : "a"(eax), "c"(ecx), "d"(edx)
        : "memory"
    );
}

// Read current PKRU register state
static inline uint32_t __rdpkru(void) {
    uint32_t eax, edx;
    uint32_t ecx = 0;

    __asm__ __volatile__(
        "rdpkru"
        : "=a"(eax), "=d"(edx)
        : "c"(ecx)
    );
    return eax;
}

// Lock-Free Single-Producer Single-Consumer (SPSC) Ring Buffer
// Uses cacheline alignment to prevent false sharing across host and agent domains.
struct alignas(CACHE_LINE_SIZE) spsc_ring {
    _Atomic uint64_t head;
    uint8_t _pad0[CACHE_LINE_SIZE - sizeof(_Atomic uint64_t)];

    _Atomic uint64_t tail;
    uint8_t _pad1[CACHE_LINE_SIZE - sizeof(_Atomic uint64_t)];

    uint64_t buffer[RING_CAPACITY];
};

// Enqueue event from isolated agent (Producer)
bool spsc_ring_enqueue(struct spsc_ring *ring, uint64_t val) {
    uint64_t current_head = atomic_load_explicit(&ring->head, memory_order_relaxed);
    uint64_t current_tail = atomic_load_explicit(&ring->tail, memory_order_acquire);

    if ((current_head - current_tail) >= RING_CAPACITY) {
        return false; // Ring buffer full
    }

    ring->buffer[current_head % RING_CAPACITY] = val;
    atomic_store_explicit(&ring->head, current_head + 1, memory_order_release);
    return true;
}

// Dequeue event from supervisor (Consumer)
bool spsc_ring_dequeue(struct spsc_ring *ring, uint64_t *val) {
    uint64_t current_tail = atomic_load_explicit(&ring->tail, memory_order_relaxed);
    uint64_t current_head = atomic_load_explicit(&ring->head, memory_order_acquire);

    if (current_tail == current_head) {
        return false; // Ring buffer empty
    }

    *val = ring->buffer[current_tail % RING_CAPACITY];
    atomic_store_explicit(&ring->tail, current_tail + 1, memory_order_release);
    return true;
}
```

