### High-Throughput Lock-Free Dispatch Engine

Building upon the low-level Driver API FFI and the aligned `MatrixPayload`, we now implement the data-plane execution harness. The objective is to eliminate all OS-level synchronization primitives—such as `pthread_mutex_t`, `std::sync::Mutex`, and condition variables—from the latency-critical kernel submission path. 

In a production GPU ingestion pipeline, latency spikes are dominated by user-to-kernel context switches, driver validation overhead, and lock contention on CPU-side submission queues. To achieve sub-microsecond launch latencies, the control-plane must decouple kernel generation from hardware dispatch using a cache-line-padded, bounded, lock-free ring buffer backed by atomic memory ordering semantics.

```rust
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
use std::cell::UnsafeCell;
use std::mem::MaybeUninit;

/// Cache-line aligned constants preventing False Sharing across distinct L1D/L2 cache lines (x86_64 / ARM64).
const CACHE_LINE_BYTES: usize = 64;
const QUEUE_CAPACITY: usize = 1024; // Must be a power of two for bitwise masking

#[repr(C, align(64))]
pub struct CacheAlignedAtomicUsize {
    value: AtomicUsize,
    _padding: [u8; CACHE_LINE_BYTES - std::mem::size_of::<AtomicUsize>()],
}

impl CacheAlignedAtomicUsize {
    pub const fn new(val: usize) -> Self {
        Self {
            value: AtomicUsize::new(val),
            _padding: [0u8; CACHE_LINE_BYTES - std::mem::size_of::<AtomicUsize>()],
        }
    }
}

/// A kernel dispatch task encapsulating compilation outputs and runtime launch parameters.
#[repr(C)]
pub struct LaunchDescriptor {
    pub function: *mut std::ffi::c_void,
    pub grid: (u32, u32, u32),
    pub block: (u32, u32, u32),
    pub shared_mem_bytes: u32,
    pub stream: *mut std::ffi::c_void,
    pub payload: MatrixPayload,
}

/// Lock-free, Single-Producer Single-Consumer (SPSC) ring buffer optimized for 
/// zero-alloc kernel dispatch. Contention-free write paths utilize Acquire-Release fences.
pub struct KernelSubmissionRing {
    head: CacheAlignedAtomicUsize, // Write pointer owned by the producer
    tail: CacheAlignedAtomicUsize, // Read pointer owned by the consumer (dispatcher)
    buffer: Box<[UnsafeCell<MaybeUninit<LaunchDescriptor>>; QUEUE_CAPACITY]>,
}

unsafe impl Send for KernelSubmissionRing {}
unsafe impl Sync for KernelSubmissionRing {}

impl KernelSubmissionRing {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        let buffer = Box::new(unsafe {
            MaybeUninit::<[UnsafeCell<MaybeUninit<LaunchDescriptor>>; QUEUE_CAPACITY]>::uninit()
                .assume_init()
        });

        Self {
            head: CacheAlignedAtomicUsize::new(0),
            tail: CacheAlignedAtomicUsize::new(0),
            buffer,
        }
    }

    /// Non-blocking enqueuing of a kernel launch descriptor.
    /// Returns `Err(descriptor)` if the ring buffer is saturated.
    #[inline(always)]
    pub fn try_enqueue(&self, desc: LaunchDescriptor) -> Result<(), LaunchDescriptor> {
        let current_head = self.head.value.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        // Acquire load ensures we see dispatcher updates to tail without reordering
        let current_tail = self.tail.value.load(Ordering::Acquire);

        if current_head.wrapping_sub(current_tail) >= QUEUE_CAPACITY {
            return Err(desc); // Ring buffer saturated
        }

        let slot_idx = current_head & (QUEUE_CAPACITY - 1);
        unsafe {
            let slot_ptr = self.buffer[slot_idx].get();
            (*slot_ptr).as_mut_ptr().write(desc);
        }

        // Release order publishes the written descriptor before head becomes visible to consumer
        self.head.value.store(current_head.wrapping_add(1), Ordering::Release);
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Dequeues a kernel launch descriptor from the ring buffer.
    /// Must be invoked strictly from the dedicated hardware dispatcher thread.
    #[inline(always)]
    pub unsafe fn try_dequeue(&self) -> Option<LaunchDescriptor> {
        let current_tail = self.tail.value.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        // Acquire load ensures we synchronize-with the producer's Release store on head
        let current_head = self.head.value.load(Ordering::Acquire);

        if current_head == current_tail {
            return None; // Buffer is empty
        }

        let slot_idx = current_tail & (QUEUE_CAPACITY - 1);
        let slot_ptr = self.buffer[slot_idx].get();
        let item = (*slot_ptr).as_ptr().read();

        // Release order informs the producer thread that the buffer slot has been cleared
        self.tail.value.store(current_tail.wrapping_add(1), Ordering::Release);
        Some(item)
    }
}
```

