### 2. Zero-Copy CXL Memory Coherence Subsystems
Compute Express Link (CXL) 3.0/3.1 specifications re-architect node-level memory hierarchies by enabling zero-copy, byte-addressable, cache-coherent memory access across disparate physical entities via `CXL.mem` and `CXL.cache` protocols. Operating over the PCIe 6.0 physical layer using PAM4 signaling (64 GT/s per lane), CXL eliminates the overhead of conventional PCIe Direct Memory Access (DMA) descriptor creation, ring-buffer allocations, interrupt processing, and host OS kernel page mapping.

```
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                    CXL 3.1 Subsystem Architecture                                |
|                                                                                                  |
| +-------------------------+     Host-Managed Device Memory     +-------------------------------+ |
| |   Host CPU / Accelerator|     (HDM) Direct Decoder Window     |   CXL 3.1 Memory Expander     | |
| | +---------------------+ |   +------------------------------+  | | +-------------------------+ | |
| | | Snoop Filter Logic  |<===>| Byte-Addressable Cacheline   |<==>| | Dynamic HDM Controller    | | |
| | +---------------------+ |   | 64-Byte Flit Granularity     |  | | +-------------------------+ | |
| | | Bias Tracking Table | |   +------------------------------+  | | | Media Controller (DDR5) | | |
| | +---------------------+ |                  ^                  | | +-------------------------+ | |
|  +-----------+-----------+                   |                  | +--------------+--------------+ |
|              |                               |                                   |                |
