While tree-based reductions exhibit lower analytical latency scaling ($O(\log N)$ versus $O(N)$), Ring AllReduce remains the industry standard for large parameter LLM synchronization due to its optimal link bandwidth utilization. Standard software-managed ring topologies suffer from severe performance degradation when subject to operating system scheduling jitter, tail latency spikes, or asynchronous PCIe transfers across ranks.

