## 3. Data Plane vs. Control Plane Protocol Dynamics

```
       HOST CONTROL PLANE                      WASM GUEST DATA PLANE
    +-----------------------+                +-----------------------+
    | Instance Orchestrator |                |  Agent Task Executor  |
    +-----------+-----------+                +-----------+-----------+
                |                                        |
 1. Compile &   | Allocate Memory & Guard Pages          |
    Attest      |--------------------------------------->|
                |                                        |
 2. Inject      | Inject Fuel Credits (e.g. 5,000,000)   |
    Fuel        |--------------------------------------->|
                |                                        |
 3. IPC Frame   | Write Task Descriptor to Shared Ring   |
    Submission  |=======================================>| (Lock-free atomic update)
                |                                        | 4. Process Frame
                |                                        |    (Local Heap Only)
                | Lock-free atomic update (Tail Advance) | 5. Yield Result
                |<=======================================|
 6. Verification|                                        |
    & Reclaim   | Attest Result Offsets in Linear Memory |
                |--------------------------------------->|
```

### Wire Format & Memory Representation

Inter-process communication uses a fixed-size, cache-line-aligned circular descriptor ring. Messages are stored within guest linear memory, eliminating serialization overheads by passing zero-copy offsets verified by the host.

```rust
#[repr(C, align(64))]
pub struct IpcDescriptor {
    pub payload_offset: u32,   // Offset relative to Wasm linear memory base
    pub payload_len: u32,      // Length of the valid frame
    pub flags: u32,            // Bitfield: [0: ACK_REQ, 1: ERR, 2: STREAM_END]
    pub correlation_id: u32,   // Monotonically increasing agent call ID
    pub timestamp_epoch_ns: u64, // Real-time timestamp for profiling
    pub _reserved: [u8; 40],   // Explicit padding to fill exactly 64-byte cache line
}

#[repr(C, align(64))]
pub struct LockFreeSpscRing {
    pub head: std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32, // Host consumer pointer
    pub _pad0: [u8; 60],                    // Prevent false sharing
    pub tail: std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32, // Guest producer pointer
    pub _pad1: [u8; 60],                    // Prevent false sharing
    pub ring_mask: u32,                     // Power-of-two capacity minus one
    pub buffer_offset: u32,                 // Offset to IpcDescriptor array in memory
}
```

### Concrete Production Rust Implementation

Below is the complete, syntactically valid Rust engine demonstrating instance allocation, fuel injection, linear memory boundary verification, and atomic ring-buffer frame dequeuing:

```rust
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU32, Ordering};
use std::sync::Arc;
use wasmtime::*;

#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
pub enum SandboxError {
    #[error("Fuel exhausted during agent execution")]
    FuelExhausted,
    #[error("Linear memory access violation: offset {offset} + len {len} > bounds {bound}")]
    OutOfBoundsAccess { offset: usize, len: usize, bound: usize },
    #[error("Lock-free queue is empty")]
    QueueEmpty,
    #[error("Wasmtime execution trap: {0}")]
    ExecutionTrap(#[from] wasmtime::Error),
}

#[repr(C, align(64))]
pub struct HostRingBufferHeader {
    pub head: AtomicU32,
    pub _pad0: [u8; 60],
    pub tail: AtomicU32,
    pub _pad1: [u8; 60],
    pub ring_capacity: u32,
    pub ring_mask: u32,
}

pub struct WasmAgentSandbox {
    engine: Engine,
    store: Store<u64>,
    instance: Instance,
    memory: Memory,
    ring_header_offset: usize,
}

impl WasmAgentSandbox {
    pub fn new(wasm_bytecode: &[u8], initial_fuel: u64) -> Result<Self, SandboxError> {
        let mut config = Config::new();
        config.consume_fuel(true);
        config.cranelift_opt_level(OptLevel::Speed);
        // Guard regions: 4GB virtual address reservation ensures hardware-enforced isolation
        config.memory_guard_size(1 << 32);

        let engine = Engine::new(&config)?;
        let module = Module::new(&engine, wasm_bytecode)?;
        let mut store = Store::new(&engine, initial_fuel);
        store.set_fuel(initial_fuel)?;

        let mut linker = Linker::new(&engine);
        // Host capability injection
        linker.func_wrap("host_env", "trap_agent", |caller: Caller<'_, u64>, code: u32| {
            log::error!("Agent explicitly trapped with error code: {}", code);
        })?;

        let instance = linker.instantiate(&mut store, &module)?;
        let memory = instance
            .get_memory(&mut store, "memory")
            .ok_or_else(|| wasmtime::Error::msg("Wasm instance missing linear memory export"))?;

        // Resolve shared ring header exported by the guest module
        let ring_header_offset = instance
            .get_global(&mut store, "__ipc_ring_ptr")
            .map(|g| g.get(&mut store).i32().unwrap_or(0) as usize)
            .unwrap_or(0x10000);

        Ok(Self {
            engine,
            store,
            instance,
            memory,
            ring_header_offset,
        })
    }

    /// Atomically dequeues a frame from the shared memory ring buffer with strict bounds checking
    pub fn try_dequeue_frame(&mut self) -> Result<Vec<u8>, SandboxError> {
        let mem_data = self.memory.data_mut(&mut self.store);
        let total_size = mem_data.len();

        if self.ring_header_offset + std::mem::size_of::<HostRingBufferHeader>() > total_size {
            return Err(SandboxError::OutOfBoundsAccess {
                offset: self.ring_header_offset,
                len: std::mem::size_of::<HostRingBufferHeader>(),
                bound: total_size,
            });
        }

        // SAFETY: Pointer is confirmed within bounds and header structure is 64-byte aligned
        let header_ptr = unsafe {
            mem_data
                .as_mut_ptr()
                .add(self.ring_header_offset) as *mut HostRingBufferHeader
        };

        let header = unsafe { &*header_ptr };
        let current_head = header.head.load(Ordering::Acquire);
        let current_tail = header.tail.load(Ordering::Acquire);

        if current_head == current_tail {
            return Err(SandboxError::QueueEmpty);
        }

        // Compute descriptor array offset located immediately after the header
        let descriptor_base = self.ring_header_offset + std::mem::size_of::<HostRingBufferHeader>();
        let slot_idx = (current_head & header.ring_mask) as usize;
        let descriptor_offset = descriptor_base + (slot_idx * 64); // 64-byte descriptor

        if descriptor_offset + 64 > total_size {
            return Err(SandboxError::OutOfBoundsAccess {
                offset: descriptor_offset,
                len: 64,
                bound: total_size,
            });
        }

        // Read descriptor fields from linear memory
        let payload_offset = u32::from_le_bytes(
            mem_data[descriptor_offset..descriptor_offset + 4].try_into().unwrap(),
        ) as usize;
        let payload_len = u32::from_le_bytes(
            mem_data[descriptor_offset + 4..descriptor_offset + 8].try_into().unwrap(),
        ) as usize;

        // Strict linear memory boundary attestation for incoming payload
        if payload_offset.checked_add(payload_len).map_or(true, |end| end > total_size) {
            return Err(SandboxError::OutOfBoundsAccess {
                offset: payload_offset,
                len: payload_len,
                bound: total_size,
            });
        }

        let payload = mem_data[payload_offset..payload_offset + payload_len].to_vec();

        // Update head pointer to release ring slot with Release ordering
        header.head.store(current_head.wrapping_add(1), Ordering::Release);

        Ok(payload)
    }

    /// Executes agent task entrypoint and verifies fuel expenditure
    pub fn execute_turn(&mut self, fuel_budget: u64) -> Result<u64, SandboxError> {
        self.store.set_fuel(fuel_budget)?;
        let entrypoint = self
            .instance
            .get_typed_func::<(), ()>(&mut self.store, "agent_main")?;

        match entrypoint.call(&mut self.store, ()) {
            Ok(_) => {
                let fuel_consumed = fuel_budget.saturating_sub(self.store.get_fuel().unwrap_or(0));
                Ok(fuel_consumed)
            }
            Err(trap) => {
                if self.store.get_fuel().unwrap_or(0) == 0 {
                    Err(SandboxError::FuelExhausted)
                } else {
                    Err(SandboxError::ExecutionTrap(trap))
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
