### Analysis of Linear Memory Boundary Attestation

WebAssembly runtimes enforce continuous address boundaries using hardware-level MMU configuration [4]. By mapping a $4\text{ GB}$ inactive address window with `PROT_NONE` immediately succeeding the dynamic base address of the guest memory, any guest out-of-bounds pointer calculation triggers an immediate hardware `SIGSEGV`. The runtime catches this signal and maps it directly to a guest trap without runtime conditional branching in generated assembly:

$$\text{Effective Address} = \text{Base}_{\text{Guest}} + (\text{Index}_{\text{Wasm}} \land \text{Offset})$$

Where $\text{Index}_{\text{Wasm}} \in [0, 2^{32}-1]$. The hardware MMU validates bounds checking in zero processor cycles, maintaining full native execution speed.

