## 5. Failure Modes & Chaos Engineering

| Failure Scenario | Root Cause Mechanic | Detection Circuitry | Mitigation & Fail-Safe Response |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Non-Terminating Turing Loop** | Malicious dynamic agent loop (e.g., `while(true){}`) | Fuel countdown monitor reaches zero ($F_{\text{remain}} = 0$) | Instant asynchronous trap generation; store context resets and caller receives `FuelExhausted` err. |
| **Corrupted Ring Pointer Overwrite** | Agent code attempts to inject malicious pointers outside linear memory | Bitwise offset validation in `try_dequeue_frame` | Host rejects frame with `OutOfBoundsAccess`, freezes guest instance, and logs cryptographic audit trail. |
| **Memory Fragmentation Exhaustion** | Agent repeatedly requests large linear memory growth (`memory.grow`) | Host-enforced maximum memory page limit (`max_pages: 1024`) | `memory.grow` returns $-1$ to guest; instance heap operations fail gracefully within guest allocator. |
| **Lock-Free Queue Head-Tail Collisions** | Producer attempts write while shared ring buffer is saturated | Full-ring invariant check: `(tail - head) == capacity` | Drop-or-backpressure signal returned to producer; host worker triggers backpressure drain. |

