## 6. Key Takeaways & Summary for Systems Architects

1. **Zero-Kernel-Crossing Isolation**: By encapsulating multi-tenant agent execution in WebAssembly linear memory sandboxes, systems architects can eliminate OS-level context switching, achieving sub-microsecond IPC and single-digit microsecond cold starts.
2. **Hardware-Enforced Memory Safety at Zero Overhead**: Utilizing $4\text{ GB}$ guard regions surrounding WebAssembly linear memory allocations offloads bounds validation to the CPU MMU, preventing memory corruption without per-operation instruction branching.
3. **Deterministic Resource Accounting via Fuel**: Injecting cycle-level instruction counters directly into JIT-compiled basic blocks provides fine-grained, reproducible CPU quotas, mitigating algorithmic complexity attacks and infinite loops.
4. **Extreme Multitenant Density**: Reducing instance memory footprints to sub-megabyte thresholds enables $10^5+$ concurrent isolated execution contexts per standard multi-socket compute node, unlocking massive density gains over container or hypervisor virtualization.

